{"proposal":{"arguments":[],"assumptions":[{"assumption_id":"node.1b01f7617ea39afc65a0bb8f.a0","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Responsibility can remain with the Product Provider while another actor performs register maintenance or technical operations.","status":"PROVISIONAL"},{"assumption_id":"node.1b01f7617ea39afc65a0bb8f.a1","provenance_refs":[],"statement":"Valuation supervision requirements are contextual comparisons unless independently applicable.","status":"PROVISIONAL"}],"bundle_hash":null,"controlled_language":"Paragraph 10 and footnote 1 principally require the Product Provider to retain full ultimate accountability for management, operational soundness and ownership records despite outsourcing. Contracts, governance arrangements and actual ability to oversee and intervene could support retained responsibility; evidence of supervision would support its exercise. Neither nominal authority nor vendor appointment establishes sound operations or proper records. Fulfillment beyond the allocation question remains unresolved without an applicable standard and facts.","family_ids":["scope"],"parent_id":null,"revision_reason":"This reading treats paragraph 10 principally as allocation of continuing accountability. An operational failure does not itself show that responsibility was transferred, although it may breach another requirement. Formal allocation alone does not establish adequate exercise of responsibility.","source_packet_hash":"d74180e126dda06342060a17b37c3227fc695e9fc0f0d5ce68b187d7cb8bc612","source_unit_ids":["dc689bdf0ffcf.u0.0","dc689bdf0ffcf.u1.224","dc689bdf0ffcf.u10.2702","dc689bdf0ffcf.u11.3045","dc689bdf0ffcf.u8.1941","dc689bdf0ffcf.u9.2169"],"subject_unit":"Paragraph 10 and footnote 1: retained accountability"},"reason":"Reserve space for unexplored families","run_id":"run.8adc12b432874c5bb1e8b4730a0ab93f"}